From acc25b7b00d1f0389d6d078045cc916488663532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:26:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gkd, rtrafd, rdnsmapd, rpunctd, rchqd, rmcpd, reaper_fwsim:
 IPv6, private /tmp, walker stand-ins that are never a device

- rtrafd: IPv6 labels and probes for dual-stack devices; skips IPv6 entries of
  the accelerator flow table (they were parsed as IPv4 and showed as "2001").
- rdnsmapd: IPv6 names (16-byte keys), maps only into a private /tmp/reaper and
  never through a link.
- rmcpd: an IPv6 listener on the router's own LAN address; .gitignore for its
  build output.
- gkd, rpunctd, rchqd: state in Reaper's private directories; scripts checked
  before they run.
- reaper_fwsim v1.10: the stand-in hosts (.123 / .124 per subnet) skip every
  address a device holds (ARP, leases, reservations) so a stand-in is never a
  real device; --used for the host suite; witness rows for the IPv6 tunnel face.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
